{
  "schema_version": "prompt-runtime.program-scenario.v1",
  "story_path": "user_stories/invocation-call-budget.md",
  "criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC1",
      "text": "When `--max-total-calls` is `18` and an `18`-call Check ends with `service-restarted` and unresolved usage, the original attempt retains its `18`-call reservation, `0` calls remain, no replacement Check is sent, and the original `unknown` uncertainty is retained."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC2",
      "text": "When `--max-total-calls` is `36` with an `18`-call per-request cap and an `18`-call Check ends with `service-restarted` and unresolved usage, `18` calls remain so at most one eligible replacement Check is permitted at `effective_max_calls: 18` while retaining prior uncertainty; any second `service-restarted` replacement on that test is refused (`restart-limit-reached`)."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC3",
      "text": "Across multiple Stories in one invocation, complete-zero pre-execution capacity refusals consume `0` calls, settled attempts consume `known_calls` and return unused allowance to the invocation pool, in-flight attempts hold candidates needing more calls (`awaiting-in-flight-settlement`) when settlement could free allowance, partial remaining allowance after settlement clamps `effective_max_calls`, and `0` remaining allowance blocks further dispatch (`call-budget-exhausted`)."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC4",
      "text": "When `--no-restart-replacement` (or `PDD_CHECK_SINGLE_ATTEMPT=1`) sets `single_attempt`, the plan disables restart replacement (`1` Check request per test, `1x` unbounded maximum) and refuses any `service-restarted` replacement (`restart-replacement-disabled`) while retaining the original `unknown` uncertainty across fresh runs, `--read`, and `--retry`."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC5",
      "text": "Pre-dispatch budget planning surfaces effective `per_request_caps`, `max_total_calls`, `restart_replacement` policy, `unbounded_maximum` versus capped `planned_maximum`, `planned_check_requests`, and `unresolved_prior_reservations` separately from the current batch's `committed_calls`, scoped strictly to `logical-interpreter-calls`."
    }
  ],
